@startuml
title Sequence Diagram - Quiz Round and Sheet Writeback

actor Teacher
participant "Teacher Portal" as TeacherUI
participant "Next.js Route Handler" as API
participant "Quiz Adjudication" as QuizFlow
participant "Student Portal A" as StudentA
participant "Student Portal B" as StudentB
participant "Activity Phase Sync (SSE)" as ActivitySync
participant "Private Redis" as Redis
participant "Google Sheets Adapter" as SheetsAccess
participant "Original Guided Notes" as Sheet
participant "Writeback Worker" as Worker

Teacher -> TeacherUI : Select Guided Notes sheet
TeacherUI -> API : POST import (spreadsheet + tab chosen by name)
API -> SheetsAccess : Read sheet via googleapis
SheetsAccess -> Sheet : Scan grid + merges (header row, numbers, answer slots)
Sheet --> SheetsAccess : Question numbers, prompts, slots
SheetsAccess --> API : Dynamic scan and mapping candidates
API --> TeacherUI : Preview with opaque slot tokens
TeacherUI -> TeacherUI : Validate count and mapping status

opt Ambiguous answer-slot mapping
  Teacher -> TeacherUI : Confirm candidate slot tokens
  TeacherUI -> API : POST mapping confirmation
  API -> SheetsAccess : Validate current scan tokens
  SheetsAccess --> API : Unique confirmed mappings
  API --> TeacherUI : Activity ready
end

alt Question count or mapping invalid
  TeacherUI --> Teacher : Show error and block start
else Questions valid
  Teacher -> TeacherUI : Tick one or more questions and open them
  TeacherUI -> API : POST open (questionNumbers[])
  API -> QuizFlow : Validate teacher and transition
  QuizFlow -> Redis : Lua: open all selected or none + XADD phase event per round
  ActivitySync -> Redis : Per-instance XREAD event Stream
  ActivitySync -> TeacherUI : Authorized phase.changed SSE
  ActivitySync -> StudentA : Phase-only SSE
  ActivitySync -> StudentB : Phase-only SSE

  par Group A submits
    StudentA -> API : POST answers[] for one open round (group from session)
    API -> QuizFlow : Validate phase and group
    QuizFlow -> Redis : Lua: accept once, sequence, winner, XADD
    Redis --> QuizFlow : Accepted order
    QuizFlow --> API : Submission receipt
    API --> StudentA : Own receipt only
  else Group B submits
    StudentB -> API : POST answers[] for one open round (group from session)
    API -> QuizFlow : Validate phase and group
    QuizFlow -> Redis : Lua: accept once, sequence, winner, XADD
    Redis --> QuizFlow : Accepted order
    QuizFlow --> API : Submission receipt
    API --> StudentB : Own receipt only
  end

  ActivitySync -> Redis : Read appended events
  ActivitySync --> TeacherUI : Live statuses and order
  note over StudentA, StudentB
    While a round is open, students only see their own status
    for that round, never other groups' answers or ranks.
    Every open question is listed and answered separately.
  end note

  Teacher -> TeacherUI : Close one question or every open question
  TeacherUI -> API : POST close (one round) / close-all
  API -> QuizFlow : Validate teacher and transition
  QuizFlow -> Redis : Lua: close each target + finalize + XADD results per round
  Redis --> QuizFlow : Immutable winner and result version
  QuizFlow --> API : Final result
  ActivitySync -> Redis : Read results.finalized event
  ActivitySync --> TeacherUI : Live result and final order
  ActivitySync --> StudentA : Closed phase and final results
  ActivitySync --> StudentB : Closed phase and final results

  opt Teacher writes results back
    Teacher -> TeacherUI : Request writeback after close
    TeacherUI -> API : POST writeback
    API -> Redis : XADD idempotent writeback job
    Redis --> API : Job queued (a failed job may be re-queued)
    API --> TeacherUI : 202 queued
    Worker -> Redis : XREADGROUP pending jobs
    Worker -> SheetsAccess : Rescan, verify structure snapshot, write RAW values
    SheetsAccess -> Sheet : Resolve target dynamically and update
    Sheet --> SheetsAccess : Write result
    SheetsAccess --> Worker : Verified writeback
    Worker -> Redis : XACK job and XADD status event
    ActivitySync -> Redis : Read writeback.status event
    ActivitySync --> TeacherUI : Final writeback status
    note over Worker, Redis
      On worker crash, XAUTOCLAIM reclaims
      idle pending jobs; idempotency prevents duplicate writes.
    end note
  end
end

@enduml
